| ShortSummary    = A year after the death of director [[Phil Coulson]], [[S.H.I.E.L.D. (Marvel Cinematic Universe)|S.H.I.E.L.D.]] is rebuilding under the leadership of [[Alphonso Mackenzie (Marvel Cinematic Universe)|Alphonso "Mack" Mackenzie]]. They investigate a series of energy anomalies formed by hostile strangers emerging from portals, one of whom gets trapped inside a wall and partially turns to concrete. In deep space, Agents [[Daisy Johnson (Marvel Cinematic Universe)|Daisy Johnson]], [[Jemma Simmons]], [[Piper (Marvel Cinematic Universe)|Piper]], and [[Davis (Marvel Cinematic Universe)|Davis]] search for [[Leo Fitz]], who was last seen in a cryofreeze chamber on a spaceship with the [[Chronicoms (Marvel Cinematic Universe)|Chronicom]] [[Enoch (Marvel Cinematic Universe)|Enoch]]; they find the spaceship abandoned and the chamber empty. Simmons learns that the chamber was created on Naro-Atzia, but the others decide to return to Earth. They are attacked by a Confederacy cruiser and, in the rush to escape, Simmons plots a course to Naro-Atzia. Mack and [[Melinda May]] recruit Dr. [[Marcus Benson]] to help found a S.H.I.E.L.D. academy and provide science support. They find coordinates on the man in concrete, [[Tinker (Marvel Cinematic Universe)|Tinker]], which lead them to a museum. The surviving hostiles are there and destroy the building to make way for their leader, [[Sarge (Marvel Cinematic Universe)|Sarge]], who looks just like Coulson.
| LineColor       = 25427D
